  "culture": [
    {
      "title": "Listen to the hills",
      "text": "Kirat heritage is part of the Mundhum journey. Choose local guides who can share their own stories, ask before recording ceremonies, and let community preferences shape the encounter.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/mundhum-trail-nepals-hidden-cultural-ridge-trek-in-2025"
    },
    {
      "title": "A living Himalayan home",
      "text": "The Everest region is also Sherpa homeland. Give monastery visits, village life and local hospitality as much respect as the mountain views; ask before photographing people or worship.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/sagarmatha-national-park"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tea, work and conversation",
      "text": "Ilam’s gardens are working landscapes. A thoughtful tea visit starts with permission, fair payment where appropriate and interest in the people who grow and make it.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/ilam"
    }
  ],
  "fieldGuide": [
    {
      "question": "Where should I begin?",
      "answer": "Choose a landscape first. Biratnagar is a useful lowland gateway, Bhadrapur connects with Jhapa and Ilam by road, and mountain regions need separate approaches. Confirm actual services for your dates.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/koshi-province"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I combine Everest, Makalu and Kanchenjunga in one short trip?",
      "answer": "Treat them as separate mountain journeys. They require distinct approaches, support, time at altitude and permits. The shorter touring routes here deliberately do not bundle them into a rushed itinerary.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/trekking-permit"
    },
    {
      "question": "What permits and guides do I need?",
      "answer": "Requirements depend on your exact route, nationality and protected or restricted area. Check Nepal Tourism Board, Department of Immigration and local park or municipal requirements with a licensed operator. Do not assume one permit covers all of Koshi.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/tims-card"
    },
    {
      "question": "When is a good time to go?",
      "answer": "Spring and autumn are common starting points for hill and mountain planning. Cooler months suit lowland nature visits. Rain, heat, snow, river levels and the elevation of the particular route matter more than a single province-wide promise.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/about-nepal/climate"
    },
    {
      "question": "Are flights, road times and prices live?",
      "answer": "No. This is a researched travel guide and planning notebook. Confirm transport operations, road access, accommodation, fees and all prices directly for your dates; keep a return buffer.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/koshi-province"
    },
    {
      "question": "What should I arrange before a trek?",
      "answer": "Agree on the exact route, daily stages, acclimatization, guides, overnight support and return arrangements. Confirm suitable equipment, communication, insurance and emergency support for the activities and elevation involved.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/tims-card"
    },
    {
      "question": "How can I visit temples and communities respectfully?",
      "answer": "Ask about access, dress, footwear and photography before entering sacred spaces. Pay hosts fairly, keep worshippers’ way clear and let local people decide how their traditions are shared.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/about-nepal/culture"
    },
    {
      "question": "What should I keep offline?",
      "answer": "Download your travel brief, confirmed addresses and contacts, booking details, required documents and an appropriate offline map. This website is an inspiration and planning tool; it is not a navigation or emergency service.",
      "source": "https://ntb.gov.np/en/koshi-province"
    }
  ],
