  "warnings": [
    "NTB Koshi overview incorrectly says12 districts and still contains old Province1 terminology. Use14 from current Assembly/provincial sources.",
    "Area conflict: official Koshi provincial profile states25,905km²; user/Wikipedia25,906km². Display approximately25,900km² or explicitly attribute25,905; do not claim a precise reconciliation.",
    "NTB pages contain dated altitude values and conflicting fee schedules. No exact peak elevations or permit prices are included.",
    "Flight routes/services and road/walking times on official tourism pages may be stale. Access wording deliberately omits guaranteed services and exact durations.",
    "Koshi Tappu crosses provincial geography: Saptari is in Madhesh. The destination card is scoped to Sunsari gateway, not a claim that all reserve land lies in Koshi.",
    "Tinjure–Milke–Jaljale spansTehrathum,Taplejung,Sankhuwasabha; district association is not an assertion that every photographed scene is in all three.",
    "Mundhum trail length/elevation differs across NTB articles; omit fixed stats. Bhojpur/Khotang ridge context is supported but precise trail variants require local planning.",
    "Pathibhara/Mukkumlung has multiple living cultural meanings; avoid treating it as belonging exclusively to a single community.",
    "Chaudandigadhi primary municipal history search was retrieved but page open timed out; the search excerpt supports historic fort. Avoid exact historical dates unsupported by retrieved content.",
    "Government administrative pages are not perfect: some still call Biratnagar a temporary capital. Current Provincial Assembly background explicitly confirms Biratnagar as selected capital.",
    "The March1,2023 naming date is supported by contemporaneous state-owned newspaper reporting plus current Assembly background; no official gazette PDF with date was retrieved.",
    "All routes are editorial travel-planning envelopes, not verified schedules, availability, bookings or high-altitude trekking programs.",
    "Rauta Pokhari replaces Chaudandigadhi as the illustrated Udayapur guide. Do not label Rauta photo as Chaudandigadhi. Bhojpur photo of Balankha and Phidim town photo are regional context, not images of the Mundhum trail or Sadhu Tar pond; label exact locations in alt/caption."
  ],
